hexia cannot be fully reversed by conventional nutritional support** because the underlying metabolic alterations and hypercatabolism persist. In contrast, **sarcopenia** is the progressive, age-related loss of skeletal muscle mass, strength, and function (independent of systemic inflammation or underlying wasting disease). **Starvation** is a state of pure caloric deprivation without inflammation, in which energy expenditure decreases and the body conserves protein; starvation is fully reversible with nutritional repletion.'),
